<title>UNITED NATIONS: U.N. approves two more Iraq contracts, total at 20.</title>
<headline>U.N. approves two more Iraq contracts, total at 20.</headline>
<dateline>UNITED NATIONS 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. oil experts on Friday approved an additional two contracts for Iraq under the oil-for-food plan, bringing the total number of contracts approved to 20, a U.N. spokesman said.</p>
<p>No details on the approved contracts were provided by the U.N. spokesman.</p>
<p>According to oil industry sources, Iraq's State Oil Marketing Organization (SOMO) is in negotiations with at least three other oil firms to lift Iraqi crude.</p>
<p>Under the oil plan, which went into effect on December 10, Iraq is allowed to sell $2 billion worth of oil over six months to buy food. medicine and other goods for its people suffering from trade sanctions imposed in August 1990.</p>
<p>--Patrick Connole, +1 212 859 1828</p>
